| ============================================================
| Splunk SPL — Noise Reduction Filters
| Developed iteratively to suppress high-volume low-signal events
| in a Windows Server 2022 / Windows 11 homelab environment
| ============================================================

| ── 1. NCSI DNS PROBE FILTER (EventCode 1014) ───────────────
| Windows Network Connectivity Status Indicator generates DNS
| query failures every ~5 minutes. Filter pattern:

index=windows (Type="Error" OR Type="Warning" OR Level=2 OR Level=3)
  NOT (EventCode=1014
    AND (QueryName="*msftncsi*"
      OR QueryName="*_msdcs*"
      OR QueryName="*_ldap*"))
| table _time, host, EventCode, Type, QueryName, Message
| sort - _time


| ── 2. ERRORS AND WARNINGS DASHBOARD BASE ───────────────────
| General error/warning feed with severity normalization

index=windows (Type="Error" OR Type="Warning" OR Level=2 OR Level=3
  OR Keywords="*Audit Failure*")
| eval Severity=coalesce(Type, LevelDisplayName, "Unknown")
| table _time, host, EventCode, Severity, Message
| sort - _time


| ── 3. PROCESS CREATION NOISE — SPLUNK SELF-MONITORING ──────
| Splunk forwarder processes generate Sysmon EventCode 1 entries.
| Filter these out to focus on actual user/system activity.

index=windows earliest=-1h EventCode=1
| eval ProcessName=mvindex(split(Image,"\\"),-1)
| search NOT ProcessName IN (
    "splunk-powershell.exe",
    "splunk-MonitorNoHandle.exe",
    "splunk-admon.exe",
    "splunk-netmon.exe",
    "splunk-regmon.exe")
| stats count by ProcessName
| sort - count
| head 20


| ── 4. LOG RECEIPT VERIFICATION ─────────────────────────────
| Confirm all three hosts are sending data and which sourcetypes

index=windows earliest=-30m
| stats count by host, sourcetype
| sort host, sourcetype
